{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340828",
      "title": "Revalidating Data To Avoid Caching Problems",
      "lectureOrder": 178,
      "videoOrder": 164,
      "sourceHash": "07308ee83e5e29e660da2e3b39b298b6ffff2d65a4460497fd05219c0fd039dd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "Now, one way of improving the user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 7.71,
          "en": "here would be to go to the Server Action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.71,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "and await these database updates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "to which I again added some delay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 16.353,
          "en": "to simulate a slower connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.03,
          "end": 23.03,
          "en": "And then thereafter, we should call the revalidatePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 28.37,
          "en": "function, which must be imported from next/cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.29,
          "end": 33.813,
          "en": "Now, what's this function about?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "Well, by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 40.14,
          "en": "NextJS caches data pretty aggressively.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.14,
          "end": 44.64,
          "en": "And we'll take a closer look at how NextJS caches data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 44.64,
          "end": 48.06,
          "en": "and what that means for you in the next section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 48.06,
          "end": 49.86,
          "en": "But what you should know here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.86,
          "end": 53.659,
          "en": "that NextJS does indeed cache page data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.659,
          "end": 55.669,
          "en": "and therefore by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.669,
          "end": 59.019,
          "en": "it will not pick up changes to data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.019,
          "end": 61.2,
          "en": "that's reflected on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.2,
          "end": 64.38,
          "en": "So of course, those changes are stored in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 66.18,
          "en": "but the page doesn't update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.18,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "just because some database data changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 73.11,
          "en": "Instead, NextJS by default will show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.11,
          "end": 78.09,
          "en": "that cached page, which is based on old data potentially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 80.493,
          "en": "and that's why this change isn't picked up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.39,
          "end": 85.47,
          "en": "Now, revalidatePath then is an important function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.47,
          "end": 89.389,
          "en": "which you should call whenever you are changing some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.389,
          "end": 92.88300000000001,
          "en": "that is shown on some page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.96000000000001,
          "end": 96.9,
          "en": "And indeed later we will also need to call it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.9,
          "end": 98.78999999999999,
          "en": "after adding a new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.78999999999999,
          "end": 100.68299999999999,
          "en": "But I'll get back to this later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.7,
          "end": 104.94,
          "en": "So for now, we should call it here to tell NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.94,
          "end": 107.72999999999999,
          "en": "that some data of some page changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.72999999999999,
          "end": 112.72999999999999,
          "en": "and we need to tell NextJS which page's data changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 114.87,
          "en": "Now attached you find a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.87,
          "end": 118.83,
          "en": "to the official revalidatePath documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.83,
          "end": 120.03,
          "en": "because it turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.03,
          "end": 123.339,
          "en": "that there are quite a few different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.339,
          "end": 126.96,
          "en": "of configuring this function or of calling this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.96,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "and of defining the path of the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 133.29,
          "en": "or pages that should be revalidated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 136.14,
          "en": "So that should be removed from the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.14,
          "end": 138.93,
          "en": "so that an updated version is shown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 142.26,
          "en": "because that's the main task of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.26,
          "end": 144.69,
          "en": "It tells NextJS that some page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.69,
          "end": 148.26,
          "en": "or pages need to be revalidated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 151.74,
          "en": "that it should not continue showing the cached versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.74,
          "end": 155.43,
          "en": "but instead create updated versions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 158.64,
          "en": "And for that, you can, for example, define the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.64,
          "end": 162.453,
          "en": "to one of your pages, for example, to the feed route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.31,
          "end": 166.47,
          "en": "With that, we would make sure that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.47,
          "end": 168.81,
          "en": "whenever the user visits that feed route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.81,
          "end": 171.27,
          "en": "an updated version is served.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.27,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "And indeed, if that's called whilst the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 178.11,
          "en": "is on the feed route, NextJS will update the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 180.84,
          "en": "behind the scenes and show an updated version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.84,
          "end": 182.313,
          "en": "of the page automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 186.36,
          "en": "And therefore, by just adding this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.36,
          "end": 190.808,
          "en": "to togglePostLikeStatus, if we go back and reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.808,
          "end": 194.91,
          "en": "and I now click here, you see initially nothing changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.91,
          "end": 199.35,
          "en": "but after a short while, this does change magically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.35,
          "end": 203.19,
          "en": "and I did not reload the page or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.19,
          "end": 205.82999999999998,
          "en": "Instead, NextJS found out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.82999999999998,
          "end": 209.97899999999998,
          "en": "that this feed page on which I was here was updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.97899999999998,
          "end": 214.26,
          "en": "or that I told it that it should revalidate that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.26,
          "end": 216,
          "en": "And since I was on that page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 218.793,
          "en": "it automatically updated it behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.78,
          "end": 222.18,
          "en": "Now here you actually also might wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.18,
          "end": 227.18,
          "en": "that NextJS is not just revalidating the feed route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 227.48,
          "end": 230.76,
          "en": "but actually maybe all pages of the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 230.76,
          "end": 234.18,
          "en": "which you can do by using just a slash here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 238.07999999999998,
          "en": "And then passing a second argument where you set a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 238.07999999999998,
          "end": 241.536,
          "en": "of layout, that essentially means that all the pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 241.536,
          "end": 245.85,
          "en": "that are wrapped by the root layout should be revalidated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 245.85,
          "end": 249.213,
          "en": "which in this case are all the pages of this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 250.71,
          "end": 253.2,
          "en": "And again, you can learn about all the details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 253.2,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "of configuring different paths, including paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 260.49,
          "en": "to dynamic segments here in that official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.49,
          "end": 263.52,
          "en": "But that's one way of revalidating that will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 263.52,
          "end": 266.223,
          "en": "that all pages pick up the latest data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 267.24,
          "end": 269.58,
          "en": "So that's an important improvement here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.58,
          "end": 272.19,
          "en": "but it's not the only improvement I want to make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 272.19,
          "end": 275.64,
          "en": "because of course with that, we still have the problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 275.64,
          "end": 279.69,
          "en": "that if I change that status, it takes a short while until",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 279.69,
          "end": 281.73,
          "en": "that change is reflected here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.73,
          "end": 283.713,
          "en": "And that's not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
